<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syagrius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 430–486/487</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syagrius was the last Roman ruler in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, governing the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soissons">Soissons</a> after the death of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegidius">Aegidius</a> in 464 or 465. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> calls him 'king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>'. In 486 he was defeated near Soissons by the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a>, fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, and was handed back to Clovis and executed.</p></div>
